/// `Fallible`: the protocol `?` resolves through for a type that is not
/// `Option` or `Result`.
///
/// `x?` returns the whole sum it was given, byte for byte, into a function of
/// the same type. So the protocol answers only which side a value is on and how
/// to read the success payload; any number of failing variants propagate intact.
///
///     impl Fallible for Http {
///         type Output = Body
///         fn isSuccess(self) -> Bool { .. }
///         fn success(self) -> Body { .. }   // total: `panic` on the failing arms
///     }
///
/// `?` calls `success` only after `isSuccess` answered true.

export protocol Fallible {
    type Output
    fn isSuccess(self) -> Bool
    fn success(self) -> Output
}
